# Template for secrets/<stage>/osa-frontend.env.j2 -- copy, fill in, then
# `ansible-vault encrypt secrets/<stage>/osa-frontend.env.j2`. This
# .example file itself is safe to commit (no real secrets in it).
#
#   cp secrets/<stage>/osa-frontend.env.j2.example secrets/<stage>/osa-frontend.env.j2
#   $EDITOR secrets/<stage>/osa-frontend.env.j2
#   ansible-vault encrypt secrets/<stage>/osa-frontend.env.j2

# Required -- the image's docker-entrypoint.d/40-generate-runtime-config.sh
# refuses to start nginx without these two (see osa-frontend/docker/
# docker-entrypoint.d/). Relative path only when backend and frontend
# share a domain (path-based split) -- once they're on separate domains
# it must be absolute, since a bare "/api" would no longer be same-origin.
API_BASE_URL={{ '/api' if backend_domain == frontend_domain else 'https://' + backend_domain + '/api' }}
APP_ENVIRONMENT={{ app_environment }}

# Optional -- graceful no-op (Google button just doesn't render) when
# unset. Same value as osa-backend.env.j2's GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID. Leave unset
# on non-production stages unless a matching OAuth client exists for this
# stage's domain.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
